# Privacy Policy

Open Messages collects nothing. No analytics, no crash reporting, no accounts, no telemetry.

Your messages, contacts and settings stay on your device. Backups are written where you choose them
and are never uploaded anywhere.

The app makes no network connection on its own. The single exception is the optional anti-phishing
list, downloaded once from The Block List Project when you enable that source in Blocking settings;
every message is matched against it on your device afterwards.
